DTSTART:20261204T163000Z
DTEND:20261204T170000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 GMT: Youth Music: Recharge Fund\, Racial Equity (up 
 to GBP 120\,000 core funding over four years)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 04 Dec 2026 at 17:00 GMT.\n\nYouth Music's Recharge Fund
 : Racial Equity gives multi-year core funding to creative organisations ac
 ross England that are led by communities who experience racial injustice a
 nd that work with children and/or young people of different ages and backg
 rounds. It is not music-only: organisations can work across a variety of a
 rt forms.\n\nOrganisation: Youth Music\nLocation: England. For creative or
 ganisations led by communities who experience racial injustice and working
  with children and/or young people.\nAward: Core funding of up to GBP 120\
 ,000 over four years per organisation\, from a total pot of GBP 2\,400\,00
 0. No application fee.\nDuration: Four years\; funded programmes start bet
 ween 1 June and 30 September 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.youthmusic.org.uk/
 funding/recharge-fund-racial-equity?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.youthmusic.org.uk/funding/recharge-fund-racial-equity?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England. For creative organisations led by communities who experie
 nce racial injustice and working with children and/or young people.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bfi-network-england-early-development-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131416Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Deadline: BFI NETWORK England: Early Development Fund (GBP 3\,000-5
 \,000 treatment awards for debut long-form writers)
DESCRIPTION:BFI NETWORK's Early Development Fund supports writers at the ve
 ry start of a debut long-form project: those who do not yet have a first d
 raft of a script (or the equivalent format for immersive work). Stage one 
 awards GBP 3\,000 to 5\,000 to produce an initial treatment setting out st
 ory\, characters\, themes and structure\, plus related materials such as a
  mood board or other visual content.\n\nOrganisation: BFI NETWORK (BFI\, N
 ational Lottery funding)\nLocation: England. Writers must be based in Engl
 and.\nAward: GBP 3\,000 to 5\,000 per project to develop a treatment (stag
 e one). Projects completed to schedule can then apply for second-stage fun
 ding to write a full first draft. National Lottery funding\; no applicatio
 n fee stated.\nDuration: Treatment stage\, then optional first-draft stage
 \n\nMore: https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/bfi-network/bfi-netwo
 rk-funding-finder/bfi-network-england-early-development-fund?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/bfi-network/bfi-network-fund
 ing-finder/bfi-network-england-early-development-fund?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England. Writers must be based in England.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shape-arts-emergent-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131416Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Shape Arts: Emergent Residency 2026/27 (Tate St Ives / Po
 rthmeor Studios)
DESCRIPTION:Shape Arts' Emergent Residency places an early-career disabled 
 artist at Porthmeor Studios in St Ives\, in partnership with Tate St Ives.
  SUPPORT: GBP 3\,000 bursary and a one-week residency (18 to 24 January 20
 27\, plus travel days)\; a wider shortlisted cohort of disabled artists re
 ceives mentoring and support.\n\nOrganisation: Shape Arts\, with Tate St I
 ves\nLocation: Porthmeor Studios\, St Ives\, Cornwall\, UK. Residency burs
 ary only for artists who live or work in Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset\; di
 sabled artists elsewhere in the UK can apply for the shortlisted cohort.\n
 Award: GBP 3\,000 bursary for the selected residency artist (restricted to
  artists living or working in Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset). Disabled arti
 sts in the rest of the UK can join the shortlisted cohort\, which brings m
 entoring and profile but no stated bursary. No application fee.\nDuration:
  One-week residency\, 18 to 24 January 2027\, plus travel days.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://www.shapearts.org.uk/Blog/apply-to-our-emergent-residency-programme
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.shapearts.org.uk/Blog/apply-to-our-emergent-residency-progr
 amme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Porthmeor Studios\, St Ives\, Cornwall\, UK. Residency bursary onl
 y for artists who live or work in Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset\; disabled 
 artists elsewhere in the UK can apply for the shortlisted cohort.
END:VEVENT
