SUMMARY:Deadline 13:00 GMT: Gasworks Residency 2027 for Artists Based in th
 e Baltics (London\, with Upe Foundation\; solo show 2028)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 02 Feb 2027 at 13:00 GMT.\n\nGasworks and the Upe Founda
 tion offer a fully funded eleven-week London residency for one contemporar
 y visual artist at a pivotal stage in their career who is based in Lithuan
 ia\, Latvia or Estonia\, as part of a multi-year partnership for artists a
 nd curators connected to the Baltic region.\n\nOrganisation: Gasworks (Lon
 don)\, with Upe Foundation\nLocation: London\, UK. For contemporary visual
  artists based in Lithuania\, Latvia or Estonia.\nAward: Fully funded 11-w
 eek residency: weekly stipend of GBP 175\, materials budget up to GBP 800\
 , private studio\, accommodation\, economy return flights and transfers\, 
 all visa costs\, plus a solo exhibition at Gasworks in 2028. No applicatio
 n fee mentioned.\nDuration: 11 weeks\, 7 July to 21 September 2027\, follo
 wed by a solo exhibition at Gasworks in July to September 2028.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency-open-call-for-artists-based
 -in-the-baltics-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency-open-call-for-artists-b
 ased-in-the-baltics-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For contemporary visual artists based in Lithuania\, 
 Latvia or Estonia.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131416Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 .\n\nOrganisation: Daiwa Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individu
 als\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running
  projects that connect the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (ty
 pical awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsis
 tence up to GBP 100 per person per day. A contribution\, not full funding.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\; activity can start from late
  May or early June 2027.\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-pr
 izes/daiwa-foundation-small-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costar-southbank-creative-intelligence-award-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131416Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261217T133000Z
DTEND:20261217T140000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 GMT: The Creative Intelligence Award 2027 (CoSTAR Na
 tional Lab x Southbank Centre)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 17 Dec 2026 at 14:00 GMT.\n\nA new co-commission from Co
 STAR National Lab and Southbank Centre to take a creative technology idea 
 that is ready to be completed\, honed or technically advanced through focu
 sed R&D\, then present it to audiences at Southbank Centre's Creative Inte
 lligence festival in autumn 2027.\n\nOrganisation: CoSTAR National Lab and
  Southbank Centre\, supported by UKRI\nLocation: UK (lead applicant must b
 e a UK-registered company\; project activity UK-based). Prototyping at Pin
 ewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Centre\, London.\nAward: GBP 50\,000
  grant (one award)\, plus up to GBP 25\,000 in AI compute and cloud credit
 s\, 2 x 5 days studio access at Pinewood Studios\, a six-week CoSTAR proto
 typing team sprint\, 3 days pre-show testing\, Southbank curatorial and pr
 oducing support\, and 20 hours of mentorship. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: R&D development through 2027\, presented at Creative Intelligence festi
 val\, Southbank Centre\, autumn 2027\n\nMore: https://www.costarnetwork.co
 .uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.costarnetwork.co.uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK (lead applicant must be a UK-registered company\; project activ
 ity UK-based). Prototyping at Pinewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Cen
 tre\, London.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:refugee-festival-scotland-opening-shot-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T131416Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Refugee Festival Scotland 2027 x Opening Shot: Open Call 
 for First-Time Filmmakers (GBP 1\,500 fee plus GBP 3\,000 production budge
 t)
DESCRIPTION:Refugee Festival Scotland (run by the Scottish Refugee Council\
 , festival 11 to 20 June 2027) and Opening Shot invite four first-time fil
 mmakers with lived experience of seeking safety to make a short film of ab
 out five minutes.\n\nOrganisation: Refugee Festival Scotland (Scottish Ref
 ugee Council) with Opening Shot\nLocation: Glasgow\, Scotland\, UK (six in
 -person workshop days in Glasgow). RESTRICTED: applicants must live in Sco
 tland and consider themselves a refugee or asylum seeker\, or have family 
 lived experience of seeking safety\; not in full-time formal education.\nA
 ward: GBP 1\,500 participation fee plus a GBP 3\,000 production budget per
  filmmaker\, with mentoring and a premiere screening at Refugee Festival S
 cotland in June 2027. Four filmmakers selected. No application fee stated.
 \nDuration: 7 months\, December 2026 to June 2027 (six workshop days Decem
 ber 2026 to March 2027\, then a 14-week supported production period).\n\nM
 ore: https://www.refugeefestivalscotland.co.uk/opening-shot-x-refugee-fest
 ival-scotland-open-call-for-first-time-filmmakers/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.refugeefestivalscotland.co.uk/opening-shot-x-refugee-festiv
 al-scotland-open-call-for-first-time-filmmakers/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Glasgow\, Scotland\, UK (six in-person workshop days in Glasgow). 
 RESTRICTED: applicants must live in Scotland and consider themselves a ref
 ugee or asylum seeker\, or have family lived experience of seeking safety\
 ; not in full-time formal education.
END:VEVENT
